State. Note `day` and `dayClock`.

Entities.

`const CLASSES` etc.

Sprites: we'll define after utility functions, before state? Sprites need palettes and functions only. We'll define build functions and then build. Hero sprites need hero color; hero defined first. Fine.

Let's write the sprite drawing functions.

#### Character drawing details

I'll use a helper `r(g,x,y,w,h,c)` and `poly(g,pts,c)`.

`drawCharFrame(g,dir,state,f,pal,opt)`:
Let's code with comments.

Pseudo:
```js
function drawCharFrame(g,dir,state,f,pal,opt){
  const side = dir.includes('E')?1:dir.includes('W')?-1:0;
  const back = dir==='N'||dir==='NE'||dir==='NW';
  const diag = dir.length===2;
  const front = !back;
  const frameStep = state==='walk' ? [1,0,-1,0][f] : 0;
  const bob = state==='idle' && f===1 ? 1 : (state==='walk' && (f===1||f===3) ? 1 : 0);
  const lean = state==='interact' ? (side||1) : state==='hurt' ? -1 : 0;
  const talk = state==='talk';
  const atk = state==='attack';
  const act = state==='interact';
  const hurt = state==='hurt';
  const cx = 16 + side + lean;
  const baseY = 44 - bob; // feet baseline
  // cape behind...
}
```

Wait, if bob subtracts from baseY, the whole character moves up. We can instead shift all y by `-bob`. Simpler: define `const y0 = -bob;` and add to all y coordinates. That's tedious. We can draw at a fixed baseline and use `g.save(); g.translate(0,-bob);` at start, then restore. Also lean: `g.translate(lean,0)`. Great. Then all drawing in base coords. Shadow not in sprite.

So:
```js
g.save();
g.translate(lean, -bob);
... draw ...
g.restore();
```
For hurt, maybe rotate? `g.translate(0,-1)` and lean. Fine.

Coordinates fixed. `cx=16`.

Cape behind:
```js
drawCape(g,pal,dir,state,f,cx);
```
Cape function uses `cx` and frame sway.

Legs and body.

Let's write the cape:
```js
function drawCharCape(g,pal,dir,state,f,cx){
 const back=dir==='N'||dir==='NE'||dir==='NW';
 const side=dir.includes('E')?1:dir.includes('W')?-1:0;
 const sway=state==='walk'?[0,1,0,-1][f]:0;
 if(back){
   poly(g,[[cx-8,19],[cx+8,19],[cx+10,33+sway],[cx+5,39],[cx,36],[cx-5,39],[cx-10,33+sway]],pal.cloakDark);
   poly(g,[[cx-6,20],[cx+6,20],[cx+7,33],[cx,37],[cx-7,33]],pal.cloak);
   r(g,cx-5,21,2,13,pal.cloakLight);
   r(g,cx+3,22,2,11,pal.cloakShade);
 } else if(side){
   const bx = cx - side*6;
   poly(g,[[bx,21],[bx-side*5,24],[bx-side*4,35+sway],[bx+side*2,33]],pal.cloakDark);
   poly(g,[[bx,22],[bx-side*3,25],[bx-side*2,33],[bx+side*2,32]],pal.cloak);
   r(g,cx-8,21,3,14,pal.cloakDark);
   r(g,cx+5,21,3,14,pal.cloakDark);
 } else {
   poly(g,[[cx-8,20],[cx-3,20],[cx-4,35],[cx-8,38]],pal.cloakDark);
   poly(g,[[cx+3,20],[cx+8,20],[cx+8,38],[cx+4,35]],pal.cloakDark);
   poly(g,[[cx-7,21],[cx-3,21],[cx-4,33],[cx-7,36]],pal.cloak);
   poly(g,[[cx+3,21],[cx+7,21],[cx+7,36],[cx+4,33]],pal.cloak);
   r(g,cx-7,22,2,11,pal.cloakLight);
   r(g,cx+5,22,2,11,pal.cloakLight);
 }
}
```
Palette keys: cloak, cloakDark, cloakLight, cloakShade. We can define.

Legs:
```js
const step = state==='walk' ? [1,0,-1,0][f] : 0;
if(side){
 const lx = cx - 2 - side*step*2;
 const rx = cx + 1 + side*step*2;
 r(g,lx,33,4,9,pal.leatherDark);
 r(g,lx,40,5,5,pal.boots);
 r(g,rx,33,4,10,pal.leather);
 r(g,rx,40,5,5,pal.boots);
 // outlines
 r(g,lx,39,5,1,pal.outline);
 r(g,rx,39,5,1,pal.outline);
} else {
 const lx = cx-5 + (step>0?1:0);
 const rx = cx+1 + (step<0?1:0);
 r(g,lx,33,5,9,pal.leather);
 r(g,lx,41,5,4,pal.boots);
 r(g,rx,33,5,9,pal.leatherDark);
 r(g,rx,41,5,4,pal.boots);
 r(g,lx,40,5,1,pal.outline);
 r(g,rx,40,5,1,pal.outline);
}
```
Torso:
```js
r(g,cx-6,19,12,15,pal.outline);
r(g,cx-5,20,10,13,pal.tunic);
r(g,cx-5,20,10,2,pal.tunicLight);
r(g,cx-5,29,10,2,pal.leather);
r(g,cx-1,29,3,2,pal.gold);
if(!back){
 r(g,cx-2,23,4,6,pal.tunicShade);
 r(g,cx-1,24,2,1,pal.gold);
 r(g,cx-1,26,2,1,pal.gold);
}
if(opt.robe){
 r(g,cx-6,19,12,24,pal.robe);
 r(g,cx-6,33,12,9,pal.robeShade);
